- op: discuss  # 7c1a
  at: '2026-08-10T13:04:16Z'  # 7c1a
  by: agent  # 7c1a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7c1a
  clock: 20  # 7c1a
  nonce: 7c1a  # 7c1a
  message: "WI-nasuf's MECHANISM REPRODUCED ON A REAL REPO AT SCALE, 2026-08-10, and it now\nhas a consumer that acts on it.\n\nUntil now kotlin's \"no call edge for an external instance-method call\" was\nestablished by reading the analyzer and by a purpose-built fixture. Measured on\nsherpa-onnx (real, 14 languages, ~117MB survey):\n\n    language     call edges   with call_construct=method\n    kotlin            2,414   0\n    java              2,924   61\n    go                2,873   1,696\n    python            9,859   5,138\n    cpp              24,871   383\n    javascript        1,749   0\n    typescript           26   0\n\nKotlin emits 2,414 call edges and ZERO method-construct edges. Its catalogue is\nmethod-shaped (30 method-keyed modules against 1 function-keyed), so essentially\nnone of it is reachable. The two modules the repo actually calls into and cannot\nadjudicate are java.io.File and java.io.FileOutputStream.\n\nWHAT CHANGED DOWNSTREAM. verify-claims now REFUSES to certify a claim in this\nstate rather than confirming it (verify_claims.method_starved_modules). The live\ndelta on a kotlin fixture that reads a socket and writes the bytes to disk is\nrc=0 `confirmed` -> rc=2 `inconclusive`. So the false-confirmation symptom of this\nclass is closed even though the emission gap itself is not; WI-nasuf stays open\nand stays bucket C.\n\nTWO SIBLING FINDINGS FILED FROM THE SAME MEASUREMENT, both in this class:\n * INV-gijis -- JS/TS populate call_construct on ZERO of 4,872 call edges, so the\n   io-boundary F3 method gate is unconditional for them. JS has the second-largest\n   sink surface (83).\n * INV-suril -- java.nio.file.Files' methods are STATIC but catalogued kind=method,\n   so the entire Files sink surface (write/copy/createDirectories/...) can never\n   match. java.io.File instance methods DO stamp correctly and DO match, which is\n   what makes the contrast diagnostic rather than speculative.\n\nMETHOD NOTE for whoever re-runs this: the survey map does NOT carry io_boundary\nmeta (it is stamped downstream), so \"did the catalogue ever match\" is NOT\nmeasurable from these artifacts. An earlier column reporting 0 tagged for every\nrepo INCLUDING a python repo that really calls os.mkdir was an instrument\nartifact, and is recorded as unmeasured rather than as a null."  # 7c1a
