  message: "PRIORITY CHANGED 2026-08-17, on owner authorisation, as part of the P0/P1 sweep. Recording the reasoning here because a re-rank that lives only in conversation is indistinguishable next session from drift.\n\nTHE GOVERNING MEASUREMENT. docs/measurements/0001-taint-flow-precision.md puts taint-flow precision at ~41% population-weighted across six real repositories. Per WI-sivuz's PRE-REGISTERED decision bands -- named before any interval was computed, so the interval cannot be used to move them -- that is the <50% band: \"precision is the headline problem and recall work should stop until it is understood.\"\n\nP1 -> P2, AND THIS IS THE LEAST CONFIDENT OF THE ELEVEN DEMOTIONS -- recorded as such rather than presented as settled. The case FOR: it is the class item over the recall family (L3 receiver evidence), so it moves with its members. The case AGAINST: it ORGANISES five other items via isbefore (WI-makij, INV-mumov, WI-nasuf, WI-zilag, INV-fibis), and a class item ranked below its own members reads oddly.\n\nReversing this one is cheap and does not disturb the rest of the re-rank; if a later session finds the L3 work is what unblocks the precision mechanisms rather than following them, put it back to P1 and say so here."  # 99df
