  message: "PHASE 6 PR 3 SHIPPED 2026-09-07 (WI-gulaz: Django reverse-relation managers + custom manager names via a project-wide relation index; instance binding for a manager's get/create/first; RelatedManager writes rowed), measured by docs/measurements/0015: pretix +27 situations / 0 lost / kserve control 0 moved; 66.7% correct, 66.7% useful (18 real fetched-row -> write pairs; 9 false: 4 check-argument at two hops, 5 structural pairings whose real carrier is an untyped instance .save() -- both filed). The class rule held again: measured through the taint path, every added situation read at source, and a pre-registered refutation checked on the production survey (0 wrong-type of 3,362 marker edges)."  # 3552
- op: discuss  # 9861
  at: '2026-09-07T10:54:31Z'  # 9861
  by: agent  # 9861
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9861
  clock: 64  # 9861
  nonce: '9861'  # 9861
  message: "PHASE 6 PR 4 SHIPPED 2026-09-07 (WI-gamas: the Django ORM instance write through the model lineage), measured by docs/measurements/0016: pretix 2 -> 75 typed `save`/`delete` sites, +11 situations / 0 lost, 72.7% correct / 72.7% useful, kserve control unmoved, 0 wrong-type on a survey-wide read-back of all 75 marker edges. The class rule held again: measured through the taint path, every added situation read at source, with the refutation conditions written before the code.\n\nA RESULT THIS CLASS SHOULD CARRY, because it is the first time an L3 fix under it was correct and still had to be held back. The measurement's third rule -- typing `super().save()` inside a model's own override, which on a real Django project is where the write actually is -- is CORRECT at the site (61 sites read back against source, 0 wrong-type) and produced 3 true findings against 20 false ones. The cause is downstream of everything this class item describes: the ADR-0017 walk advances along the django-orm-dispatch linker's `dispatches_to` edge as if it carried a value, so a sink placed inside a model method is reachable from any function that merely mentions the class. Measured: 33 of 33 class-node hops the walk traversed sat on such a pair, the 16,010 containment-only pairs were never crossed, and withholding the rule takes those hops from 33 to 0.\n\nSO THE CHAIN THIS ITEM DESCRIBES NEEDS A FIFTH LINK, and it is not a catalogue or an analyzer link. L1 the row exists, L2 the analyzer emits, L3 the edge carries receiver evidence, L4 the F3 gate accepts -- and now L5: THE WALK MUST ADVANCE ONLY ALONG EDGES THAT CARRY A VALUE. An L3 fix can be correct at every one of the first four links and still produce false findings at the fifth. The 2026-09-04 entry on this thread already established that an L3 fix must be measured through the taint path rather than io-boundaries chain counts; this adds that the taint path itself can manufacture the finding, so the read-back at source is not optional and a per-situation path shape must be inspected, not just the verdict.\n\nFiled as a new invariant with the measurement as evidence; the withheld rule is filed behind it with a written re-open trigger."  # 9861
- op: discuss  # 5d7a
  at: '2026-09-08T03:17:36Z'  # 5d7a
  by: agent  # 5d7a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5d7a
  clock: 65  # 5d7a
  nonce: 5d7a  # 5d7a
  message: "THE ESCAPE-CLOSING FAMILY'S SUPPRESSION SIGN IS NOW MEASURED, and it is\nnon-zero. Recorded here because this item is a member of that family and its\nown record still reads as though the effect is zero.\n\nINV-busis' declared-sanitizer arm ran 2026-09-07 (dev f57e589a21; full record\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/busis_suppression_09072026/). The five-repo\n\"barrier_walks = 0\" that the family's zero rests on was measuring the DEFAULT\nSANITIZER CATALOGUE, not the code path. With nine ordinary laundering functions\ndeclared under `extra_catalogs: sanitizers:`, barrier walks go 0 -> 4\n(alertmanager), 0 -> 122 (beads), 0 -> 6 (kserve). And with a population, the\nceiling arm (`_use_site_terminates` -> True, every escape closed at once) MOVES\nFINDINGS for the first time: on beads it converts 77 section 3a walks and ONE\nbarrier walk from None to False, and the run goes\n\n    violated 6 / sanitized 351 / evidence 230\n -> violated 6 / sanitized 352 / evidence 225\n\n`violated_claims` is unchanged everywhere, exactly as the section 3a predicate\n(`walk_result is True`) requires. What moves is the barrier arm, where a False\nearns `sanitized` and a sanitized flow is DROPPED from the claim's violation set\n(#214).\n\nWHAT THIS MEANS FOR WORK ON THIS ITEM: closing escape sites is not free and its\nonly reachable effect on findings today is to DELETE them. A change in this\nfamily should ship with its own declared-sanitizer suppression arm, not with a\ndefault-catalogue run that reports the catalogue's zero as the change's zero.\n\nCAVEAT CARRIED: three repositories, two languages, and a sanitizer set chosen to\nCREATE population (`fmt.Sprintf` does not neutralise untrusted input). The\nMAGNITUDE is an artefact of the declaration; the DIRECTION and the existence of\nan effect are the interpretable parts. A project that declares no sanitizers\nstill gets zero."  # 5d7a
