  nonce: 998f  # 998f
  message: "TABLE CORRECTED TO ITS OWN INSTRUMENT, 2026-09-09. `scripts/measure-catalogue-exposure.py` landed in PR 6b72c22384 with 12 tests, and the exposure block in this description is now its VERBATIM OUTPUT rather than a paste from the lab prototype.\n\nWHAT MOVED, disclosed because I installed the wrong numbers earlier today: the prototype deduplicated by qualified_name where the shipped script counts RAW ROWS. c R2-only 16 -> 22, cpp 16 -> 22, elixir 133 -> 134, erlang 59 -> 60, go R1-only 30 -> 45 with dual 35 -> 40, objc R1-only 123 -> 125, python R2-only 84 -> 91. The R2-only total moves 392 -> 397.\n\nNO VERDICT MOVES. All five dismissed languages remain R1 = 0 with R2 > 0; objc remains a pure receiver-syntax cell; C remains the confirmed fail. The route column now reads `both` rather than `receiver` for kotlin/scala/java, because each carries a small R2-only count (3/5/3) that the prototype's hand-assigned label ignored -- that is a genuine correction, not a formatting change.\n\nWHY THIS MATTERED ENOUGH TO REDO AN HOUR-OLD EDIT: a table that disagrees with the tool that regenerates it is exactly the drift the tool was landed to stop, and it would have been the THIRD time this item's exposure figures were restated by hand. The block now carries a REGENERATE, DO NOT RESTATE instruction naming the command.\n\nThe two counts are both reported by the script (`r2_ambiguous` rows and `r2_distinct` qualified names) precisely so this cannot recur silently -- that is the disclosed prototype defect from the phase 1 entry, now fixed in the shipped instrument rather than only noted."  # 998f
