  nonce: 300a  # 300a
  message: "T0b DRAIN — ELIXIR CELL (1 of 2) DRAINS. WI-kigub, PR #908, merged e696785da4.\nRecord: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/kigub_09102026/.\n\nClosed on CORRECTNESS, per the owner's 2026-09-10 drain criterion (ruling (c)):\nthe fix is right, it loses nothing, and the newly-resolved rows were read back\nagainst source. No per-cell primitive delta is demanded here; the ledger carries\nthat at T0c.\n\nThe class instance: an Elixir call site of a catalogued I/O primitive written in\nthe ATOM receiver syntax (`:ets.insert`, `:httpc.request`) produced NO call edge\nat all, so no receiver evidence downstream could reach the catalogue entry. This\nis the L2 limb of the statement, and the atom form is the ONLY syntax by which\nElixir can call an Erlang/OTP module, so the whole OTP surface was invisible.\n\nCORRECTNESS EVIDENCE (phoenix-framework, PYTHONHASHSEED=0, both arms\nreproducing themselves exactly, elixir.py blob asserted at arm BEGIN and END):\n  - +122 call edges over 25 distinct OTP modules; VANISHED 0; symbols 0/0.\n  - io-boundaries 250 -> 277 chains, 52 -> 65 distinct elixir primitives,\n    primitives LOST 0.\n  - The item's own six filed rows re-run individually: all six 0-before,\n    >0-after, five matching their filed site counts exactly.\n  - The L3 half was decided by executing `_module_matches` rather than\n    reasoning about it: the module slot is emitted WITHOUT the leading colon,\n    because `catalog='ets'` vs `hint=':ets'` is False and an edge that exists\n    but matches nothing is the exact defect this invariant names.\n\nCONTRIBUTION TOWARD T0c's LEDGER, recorded here so T0c does not have to\nre-derive it. This is the first drained cell to move user-visible answers:\n  - `db_read` (0 -> 8) and `db_write` (0 -> 10) appear as boundary KINDS\n    phoenix-framework had NEVER reached; all 18 chains have an `ets` sink.\n  - `verify-claims` findings 19 -> 31, and TWO verdicts move from\n    `inconclusive` to `violated` — untrusted-input-no-database (ev=4,\n    origins db_read:4) and host-secret-no-network (ev=1, origins env_read:1).\n    They were inconclusive because hypergumbo could not see `:ets` or `:httpc`\n    at all and correctly said so.\n  - All five findings adjudicated against source: 5/5 structurally correct,\n    0 wrong. Usefulness is weak and stated as such — four are a config cache\n    reading and writing its own ETS table, and the fifth is WI-gohok's\n    already-ruled config-flow category. Elixir is `dataflow_capable: false`,\n    so all 31 findings remain structural/approximate.\n\nROSTER: 8 of 10 cells shipped. LEFT: elixir WI-kafor, haskell WI-lokun.\nThe arc file's \"(grammar NOT installed locally)\" note against the two elixir\ncells is REFUTED — the analyzer reaches elixir through\n`tree_sitter_language_pack`, not `tree_sitter_elixir`, and runs fine. WI-kafor\nis actionable now; a note to that effect is on it."  # 300a
