  message: "T0b DRAIN — ELIXIR CELL (2 of 2) DRAINS. WI-kafor, PR #910, merged 61efc94b0e.\nRecord: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/kafor_09102026/.\n\nClosed on CORRECTNESS per the owner's 2026-09-10 drain criterion. **9 of 10\ncells shipped; only haskell WI-lokun remains.**\n\nThe class instance, and it is the OTHER direction from WI-kigub's: the call\nsite DID produce an edge and the edge went to the wrong place. A\nmodule-qualified call to a catalogued module (`Logger.error`) was resolved by\nBARE NAME to a first-party function, so it never reached its catalogue entry --\n202 such edges on phoenix-framework, including bindings into EEx GENERATOR\nTEMPLATES and onto a **defp**, which Elixir cannot call cross-module at all.\n\nCORRECTNESS EVIDENCE (phoenix, PYTHONHASHSEED=0, both arms self-reproducing,\nblob asserted BEGIN and END):\n  - 208 edges REDIRECTED; total unchanged at 11,222; symbols unchanged.\n  - ALL 206 lost first-party edges adjudicated: 200 refused because the\n    expanded module is not a project module; 6 read back against source and\n    all corrections. **REAL LOSSES: 0.**\n  - The item's own filed rows re-run: `Logger.error` (filed 10 sites, actually\n    14 across TWO template files) and `Logger.info` (filed 3) both now reach\n    the Logger catalogue rows.\n  - Measured at L4 on findings, as this item required.\n\nCONTRIBUTION TO T0c's LEDGER — the second drained cell to move user-visible\nanswers, and it moves a DIFFERENT limb from WI-kigub's:\n  - `logging` chains 53 -> 64; `process_send` 0 -> 5, a boundary KIND phoenix\n    had never reached. Primitives 65 -> 68, **0 lost**: `Logger.error` (8),\n    `Logger.info` (3), `supervisor.start_link` (5).\n  - `host-secret-no-logging` violated ev=5 -> ev=7; every other verdict\n    byte-identical; 0 evidence lost. Both new findings read back against\n    source and both correct.\n\nTWO THINGS T0c SHOULD CARRY FORWARD FROM THIS CELL:\n  1. WHAT SHIPPED IS NOT WHAT WAS PRE-REGISTERED. The exact module-ownership\n     gate was built and measured first; it is necessary and NOT sufficient, so\n     the bare-name resolution was removed outright and the gate helper deleted\n     as dead code. A gate decides WHICH inputs reach a mechanism; if the\n     mechanism is wrong, gating it better still ships the defect.\n  2. A SUBSTRING TEST CAN BE LOAD-BEARING BY ACCIDENT. Removing it exposed two\n     alias-reading gaps that had been invisible for as long as the bug existed\n     -- the brace form `alias A.{B}` (71 true edges) and first-component\n     expansion (29) -- and the pre-registered control is the only reason they\n     were found rather than shipped as losses."  # 8886
