  message: "**T0b IS COMPLETE — 10 OF 10 CELLS DRAINED.** haskell WI-lokun was the last.\nRecord: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/lokun_09112026/.\n\nROSTER, all shipped and merged:\n  python      INV-mumov  #890 (ADR-0053)      objc      WI-garar   #869/#870\n  scala       WI-sigog   #867 + WI-pokam #892  swift     WI-dodop   #877\n  javascript  WI-vihop #894 · WI-kikar #898 · WI-dosuh #903\n  elixir      WI-kigub   #908 · WI-kafor #910\n  haskell     WI-lokun   (this PR)\n\nEach drains on CORRECTNESS per the owner's 2026-09-10 ruling (c): the fix is\nright, it loses nothing, and the newly-resolved rows were read back against\nsource. T0c carries the primitive demand ONCE over the drained set.\n\nWHAT THE DRAINED SET ALREADY SUPPLIES FOR T0c's LEDGER, so T0c does not\nre-derive it. The elixir and haskell cells alone moved user-visible answers in\nthree different ways:\n  * FOUR boundary KINDS appeared on repositories that had never reached them --\n    `db_read` (0->8) and `db_write` (0->10) and `process_send` (0->5) on\n    phoenix-framework, and `logging` rose 53->64 there and gained\n    `Prelude.print` on servant.\n  * TWO verdicts moved from `inconclusive` to `violated` on phoenix\n    (untrusted-input-no-database ev=4, host-secret-no-network ev=1) and a third\n    gained evidence (host-secret-no-logging ev=5->7). They were inconclusive\n    because hypergumbo could not see `:ets` or `:httpc` AT ALL and correctly\n    said so.\n  * PRIMITIVES: phoenix 52 -> 68 distinct elixir primitives, servant 15 -> 16\n    (kind, primitive) pairs. **ZERO lost in either language.**\n  * SEVEN new findings adjudicated against source across the two elixir cells\n    and three chains across the haskell one: **10/10 correct, 0 wrong.**\n  * Earlier cells: WI-lafom moved AFNetworking primitives 12->21 and net_recv\n    0->2; WI-dodop moved 1 newly reachable primitive and 2 substantive chains;\n    INV-mumov moved 0 for +2,943 edges.\n\nWHAT REMAINS FOR T0c, unchanged: the two single arms over the DRAINED SET --\nthe declared-sanitizer suppression arm (owner 2026-09-09) and the\nprimitive-delta demonstration (owner 2026-09-10) -- and then INV-linub\nsatisfied on PER-LANGUAGE behavioural evidence rather than on the measurement\nbeing finished.\n\nA PATTERN THAT HELD IN EVERY SINGLE CELL, five for five in the last two days\nand worth stating as a rule rather than an observation: **THE FILED ITEM NAMED\nFEWER SHAPES THAN EXIST.** WI-pokam named one annotation shape and there were\nthree; WI-vihop listed four spellings and the fifth is the one nextjs uses;\nWI-kikar named two rows and enumeration found eight calls; WI-dosuh named one\nreceiver spelling and parity-probing found four; WI-kigub named one dot shape\nand the grammar has six; WI-kafor named one sub-mechanism and instrumenting\nfound two; WI-lokun named two example files and there are three. PROBE THE\nFAMILY BEFORE FIXING THE NAMED INSTANCE."  # b238
