  clock: 91  # 0db1
  nonce: 0db1  # 0db1
  message: "T0c COMPLETE — BOTH ARMS RAN, BOTH CONTROLS FIRED, AND THIS ITEM IS SATISFIED ON\nPER-LANGUAGE BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE. Record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/t0c_09112026/\n(PLAN.md pre-registered before any number, plus three dated addenda appended\nrather than edited); published as measurement 0029.\n\nARM B — THE PRIMITIVE DEMAND (owner ruling 2026-09-10, the ledger half).\n\nSix of the seven drained languages reached a primitive they had not reached\nbefore; elixir moved TWO claim verdicts (`inconclusive` -> `violated`) and\njavascript moved EVIDENCE within a verdict that was already `violated` (4 -> 7),\nwhich is a user-visible answer moving but is NOT a verdict change and is not\ncounted as one; ZERO primitives were lost anywhere.\n\n  python      INV-mumov    NO new kind (16 -> 16), io_tag_rate +31.1%   inherited\n  objc        WI-lafom/WI-garar   12 -> 21 and 19 -> 22, net_recv 0->2  inherited\n  scala       WI-sigog/WI-pokam   rows 0 -> 13 (sbt), 1 -> 2 (lila)     inherited (0024)\n  swift       WI-dodop     +1 (NonBlockingFileIO.readChunked)           inherited (0028)\n  javascript  WI-vihop/WI-kikar/WI-dosuh   +5, 0 lost, evidence 4->7    MEASURED AT T0c\n  elixir      WI-kigub/WI-kafor   +16 and FOUR new boundary KINDS       inherited\n  haskell     WI-lokun     +1 (Prelude.print)                           inherited\n\nSIX ROWS ARE INHERITED AND ONE WAS MEASURED HERE, and the table says so per row.\nThat is deliberate: the demand was for ONE demonstration over the SET, and six\nof seven already carried a primitive delta from the cell's own live A/B with a\ncorrect per-cell baseline. What was genuinely missing was javascript — WI-vihop\nstates in as many words that it closed \"with no per-cell primitive [delta]\" —\nso javascript is the arm that ran.\n\nTHE JAVASCRIPT ARM. Whole-tree A/B, OFF `fa20fe2048` (parent of the first\njavascript drain commit) vs ON `e3b448b616`, each pinned in its own git worktree\nand reached through PYTHONPATH. Subject workadventure (254 MB): 5 distinct\n(lang, kind, primitive) triples gained, 0 lost; `host-description-no-network`\nevidence 4 -> 7; 4 of 4 distinct new primitives read back against source and\nCORRECT. Per-cell attribution: all five gains are WI-kikar's, WI-vihop shows as\n`fs.promises.readFile` 1 -> 2 chains, WI-dosuh emits registrations and surfaces\nno new primitive here.\n\nONE FINDING AGAINST THE CATALOGUE RATHER THAN THE ANALYZER, filed separately:\nthe `process.on` row's own note says `process.on('message', ...) for IPC from\nparent`, but the row matches ANY event name and both live sites are\n`unhandledRejection` / `uncaughtException`. The emission is right; the row\nover-matches, so one of the five reaches `ipc_recv` on evidence that does not\nsupport it.\n\nNO-LEAKAGE CONTROL (P3, pre-registered, COULD have failed): modsecurity — zero\n.js/.ts, zero .ex/.exs, zero .hs — is BYTE-IDENTICAL through both arms\n(io.json md5 0dd362492d…, vc.json md5 0fe07a57e7… in both). The arms differ by\nthe javascript cell and by nothing else.\n\nARM A — THE DECLARED-SANITIZER SUPPRESSION ARM (owner ruling 2026-09-09).\n\n    metric              A control   B ceiling   |  NO DECLARATION\n    barrier walks / F        5/0         5/0    |       0/0\n    sanitized flows          158         158    |         0\n    violated claims            7           7    |         7\n    evidence                 202         201    |       204\n    instrument control  LIVE — 3 walk(s) left 'none'\n\nTWO THINGS WERE BEING CONFLATED UNDER \"SUPPRESSION\" AND THE PAIR OF RUNS\nSEPARATES THEM. (1) A DECLARATION suppresses, heavily: seven declared python\nsanitizer functions take pretix from 0 to 158 sanitized flows. (2) THE DRAIN\nDOES NOT: inside the declared arm, closing EVERY escape site at once moves\nsanitized_flows and violated_claims by 0, at a cost of one evidence item. Arm B\nis a CEILING, so that is a proof about the whole family — no INV-linub member\ncan suppress a finding through this channel.\n\nTHE PRE-REGISTERED CONTROL WAS NOT FALSIFIABLE AS WRITTEN AND WAS REPLACED\nBEFORE THE READING WAS USED (addendum 2). `barrier_walks > 0` is satisfiable by\nthe built-in catalogue alone, so it could not fail. The no-declaration arm makes\nit a DIFFERENCE: barrier_walks 5 vs 0, sanitized_flows 158 vs 0.\n\nTHE MISSPELLING TRAP THE 2026-09-09 RULING WARNED ABOUT IS CLOSED, verified live\nrather than restated: `taint_sanitizers:` now exits 2 with \"unknown\nextra_catalogs field(s): 'taint_sanitizers' … Did you mean: sanitizers?\".\nINV-sisod closed it after the ruling was written.\n\nWHY SATISFIED, AND AGAINST WHICH BAR. Ten cells drained on CORRECTNESS per the\n2026-09-10 ruling (c); this ledger owed ONE demonstration that the drain moved\nuser-visible answers, and the standard was fixed in advance (P4: discharged if\nat least one row moved; NOT discharged if every row is \"more sites tagged, no\nnew type\"). Six rows moved a primitive and elixir moved two verdicts. Both halves are\nbehavioural: per-cell correctness adjudicated against source, and a live\nmeasurement over the drained set. Nothing here is satisfied on \"measurement\ncomplete\", which is the INV-nufob shape this item's own closure clause bars.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT ESTABLISH, so the closure is not read as more than it is: not\na precision claim; n_effective per language row is ONE repository (two for scala\nand objc); Arm A is pretix alone (apollo-server produced NO WALKS and is\nexcluded from the denominator rather than folded in as a zero); and one of\njavascript's five new primitives rests on a catalogue row that over-matches."  # 0db1
